{{!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     home/subscribe-form — the hero's inline signup.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     data-members-form="subscribe" is Ghost's own hook: its members script
     intercepts the submit, posts the address, and flips the elements marked
     data-members-success / data-members-error. No JavaScript of ours, and no
     action URL to keep correct.

     BOTH RESPONSE MESSAGES EXIST UP FRONT, hidden. A live region created at
     the same moment as its message announces nothing — the region has to be
     in the DOM before the text lands in it.

     .ns-cta-card__form carries display:flex and `flex: 1` on .ns-input, so
     the field and the button lay out with no utility of their own. The width
     cap and the top margin are the two things NSDS has no class for here:
     .ns-hero__actions would bring a second flex context and fight the form's.
     ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}
<form class="ns-cta-card__form mt-6 max-w-104" data-members-form="subscribe">
    <label class="ns-visually-hidden" for="hero-email">{{t "Email address"}}</label>
    <input id="hero-email" class="ns-input" type="email" name="email"
           autocomplete="email" required
           placeholder="{{t "you@example.com"}}" data-members-email>
    <button class="ns-btn ns-btn--white" type="submit">
        {{> "icons/paper-plane-tilt"}} {{t "Subscribe"}}
    </button>
</form>

<p class="ns-field__help" data-members-success role="status" hidden>
    {{t "Check your inbox — the confirmation link is on its way."}}
</p>
<p class="ns-field__error" data-members-error role="alert" hidden>
    {{t "That did not work. Check the address and try again."}}
</p>
